cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "pyselectal: Python selection of alignments by 5′-end type"
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-01-01"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/nikitin-p/pyselectal"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nikitin
    given-names: Pavel
  - family-names: Sidorov
    given-names: Sviatoslav
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - genomics
  - transcription start site
  - TSS
  - CAGE
  - RNA-seq
  - BAM
  - SAM
  - alignment filtering
abstract: >-
  Pyselectal is a command-line tool for filtering genomic alignments
  in BAM, SAM, and CRAM formats by the length and sequence of soft-clipped
  or mapped 5′-ends. It supports single-end and paired-end reads and is
  designed for NGS pipelines focused on transcription start sites.
